CloudBurrow patch 100 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1816). Applies after patch 0098; needs
googlesqlite patch 0099.

A NULL query parameter was bound as a Go nil, which has no type, so
`SELECT @p` with a NULL STRING, DATE or NUMERIC was an INTEGER. An ARRAY
parameter's elements were bound as their REST text, so an ARRAY<DATE>,
ARRAY<NUMERIC> or ARRAY<BYTES> was an ARRAY of STRING, and a STRUCT as a
Go map, typed STRING, its fields in no order. BigQuery types each as
declared (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/parameterized-queries).
They are bound as googlesqlite.TypedParameter (googlesqlite patch 0099):
a NULL of its type, an ARRAY of its element type, a STRUCT of its fields'
types in their order (a missing field, or a scalar with no value but a
STRING or BYTES, a NULL). A type with a RANGE in it, or a STRUCT field
with no name, is bound as before.

server/cloudburrow_typed_null_array_struct_parameters_test.go
(TestTypedNullArrayStructParameters: a NULL of every scalar type, an
ARRAY, a STRUCT and an ARRAY of STRUCTs, positional and named, in the
select list; a STRUCT's fields; a NULL STRUCT).

